    "2024_csat_35": [
      {
        "num": 1,
        "mark": "①",
        "text": "Although we’d like to think that our minds are sharp enough to always make good decisions with the greatest efficiency, they just aren’t."
      },
      {
        "num": 2,
        "mark": "②",
        "text": "In reality, the brain arrives at an intersection of four or five possible things to say and sits idling for a couple of seconds, considering the options."
      },
      {
        "num": 3,
        "mark": "③",
        "text": "Making a good decision helps you speak faster because it provides you with more time to come up with your responses."
      },
      {
        "num": 4,
        "mark": "④",
        "text": "When the brain stops sending navigational instructions back to the mouth and the mouth is moving too fast to pause, that’s when you get a verbal fender bender, otherwise known as filler."
      },
      {
        "num": 5,
        "mark": "⑤",
        "text": "Um, ah, you know, and like are what your mouth does when it has nowhere to go."
      }
    ],
